Project Title

Customer Segmentation Analysis using K-Means Clustering

Objective

The objective of this project is to analyze customer behavior and purchasing patterns to divide customers into different segments using clustering techniques. This helps businesses create targeted marketing strategies and improve customer satisfaction.

Dataset

The dataset contains customer information such as:

Customer ID
Income
Purchase history
Spending behavior
Product purchases
Tools and Libraries Used
Python
Pandas
NumPy
Matplotlib
Seaborn
Scikit-learn
Jupyter Notebook
Steps Performed
1. Data Collection
Loaded the customer dataset using Pandas.
2. Data Exploration and Cleaning
Checked dataset structure
Handled missing values
Removed unnecessary columns
3. Descriptive Statistics

Calculated:

Average spending
Purchase frequency
Customer behavior statistics
4. Feature Engineering

Created features such as:

Total Spending
Total Purchases
5. Data Scaling
Standardized numerical features using StandardScaler.
6. Customer Segmentation
Applied K-Means clustering algorithm
Used the Elbow Method to determine optimal clusters
7. Data Visualization

Created:

Scatter plots
Cluster visualization charts
Customer segment comparison plots
8. Segment Analysis
Analyzed characteristics of each customer group
Compared spending and purchasing behavior
Key Insights
Some customers are high spenders with frequent purchases.
Certain customers have low spending patterns.
Customer groups can be targeted differently for marketing.
Recommendations
Offer premium products to high-value customers.
Provide discounts and offers to low-engagement customers.
Use personalized marketing strategies for different customer segments.
Outcome

This project provided practical experience in:

Clustering algorithms
Customer segmentation
Data preprocessing
Data visualization
Business analytics
Conclusion

The project successfully segmented customers based on purchasing behavior using K-Means clustering. The analysis can help businesses improve marketing strategies and customer engagement.